  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_023",
  "text": "Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 8.0 Heritage Conservation Areas Map\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): Buildings that make a positive contribution to the character of the HCA should be retained\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): Demolition of buildings that positively contribute to the character of the HCA will generally not be supported\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): Original building materials such as brick, sandstone, timber and slate should be retained and repaired where possible.\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): New development should respect the scale and massing of existing buildings in the HCA.\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): New building facades should be compatible with the architectural style and materials of existing buildings in the HCA.\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): Roof forms and pitches of new development should be compatible with existing buildings in the HCA.\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): Landscaping should be used to enhance the character of the HCA.\n\nClause N/A - heritage (development_control): Fences and walls should be compatible with the architectural style and materials of existing buildings in the HCA.\n\n",
  "metadata": {
    "document_name": "Marrickville DCP 2011 - 8.0 Heritage Conservation Areas Map",
    "extractions_count": 8
  }
